{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs71Pb4fVVFp5Dh75cbo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed both bugs in `sched/core.py`, and `tests/test_sched.py` passes (1 test). The function signature is unchanged.\n\n**Root causes**\n1. **Skipped day after 22:00 UTC.** The old code took `now.date()`, which is the UTC calendar day, not the day in `tz`. At 23:30 UTC on June 1 it is already June 2 in Berlin, but the code built its candidate on June 1. That candidate was already past, so it added a day and returned June 2 instead of the correct June 3.\n2. **Off by an hour around DST.** To move to the next day, it added `timedelta(days=1)` to the candidate in UTC. That moves 24 elapsed hours, not one local calendar day. On the 23-hour or 25-hour days around a DST change, the wall-clock time shifts by an hour.\n\n**Fix.** The function now takes the date in `tz` and builds the wall-clock time on that date. It returns the first candidate strictly after `now`, and if there isn't one it moves to the next local calendar day and tries again.\n\nI also decided what happens to a time that doesn't exist on the DST spring-forward day: it moves to the first valid time after the gap. Asking for 02:30 Berlin on 2026-03-29 therefore returns 03:30 +02:00. I picked this rather than skipping to the next day. For a time that occurs twice in the autumn, it returns the first occurrence.\n\nI checked a few DST cases by hand in Berlin and they came out as expected:\n- **Day before the gap:** from 2026-03-28 12:00 UTC, asking for 02:30 returns 03:30 +02:00 on March 29.\n- **During the gap day:** from 2026-03-29 00:30 UTC, asking for 02:30 also returns 03:30 +02:00 on March 29.\n- **After the change:** from 2026-03-29 12:00 UTC, asking for 01:00 returns March 30 at 01:00 +02:00, with the correct offset.\n\nI did not add DST regression tests to the test file. Say so if you want them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11086,"cache_read_input_tokens":47337,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11086},"output_tokens":683,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"082d110c-fe26-4546-97fb-2db593094ee3","uuid":"732b6ecd-b542-48ec-8810-d2a3058aa045","timestamp":"2026-10-09T18:04:00.413Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs71PGxq4qUDpnmJeAx6"}
